FLEX Canvas may be used independently of Laravel, Filament and FLEX Fields.

3.2 Inherited scope. The applicable FLEX Fields license and accepted confirmation
control the covered licensee/entities, number and identity of products, hosting or
distribution rights, duration, update entitlement, transfers, refunds and termination.
For example, a Single Product grant covers that product; an Unlimited Company grant
covers that licensee's qualifying products; an Enterprise Group grant covers its
qualifying entities and products. Inclusion does not convert a narrower existing
grant into unlimited, group, OEM or redistribution rights. Previously issued grants
retain their agreed terms and are not narrowed or repriced by this document.

3.3 Covered operations. Within that scope You may integrate, modify and operate
FLEX Canvas in the covered applications, including charging for authorized hosted
SaaS access. Development, staging, QA, CI, backups and disaster recovery copies of
covered applications require no extra license. There are no additional Canvas seat,
CPU, server, user or tenant fees. More products/entities require an appropriate
underlying grant; unlimited users do not mean unlimited legal entities or products.

3.4 Special distribution. Customer installations, OEM, sublicensing, SDK resale,
reusable templates, starter kits and other independent distributions require express
written rights covering that activity. A paid FLEX Fields license includes them
only if its accepted terms expressly grant them. A client-owned bespoke application
may instead obtain its own applicable license from the Copyright Holder, with its
agency acting solely as Authorized Personnel. That is not an agency-wide resale grant.

3.5 Confirmation. Keep the FLEX Fields license confirmation and payment evidence.
A public package download or a payment unrelated to a valid grant is not evidence
of commercial rights. A separately agreed written Canvas license may also authorize
commercial use; its expressly agreed scope prevails for that grant. No separate
